# Secrets. The only env file that is ever committed is .env.example, which
# holds placeholders. Everything real — Clerk keys, Firebase config, service
# accounts — lives in .env locally and in Vercel's environment variables in
# production. Firebase *web* config is public by design, but the Clerk secret
# key and any service account are not, and none of them belong in git.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.vercel
